From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:34:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: mock Mac Chrome Widevine capability access natively

Expose secure Window-only requestMediaKeySystemAccess and native
MediaKeySystemAccess, MediaKeys, MediaKeySession and MediaKeyStatusMap
interfaces following Chromium 155 IDL. Negotiate a bounded synthetic
com.widevine.alpha profile: cenc MP4 AVC/AAC, software robustness and
temporary sessions, with no persistent state or distinctive identifiers.
The profile targets the MacBook Neo persona; it does not inspect host
hardware or load a Widevine CDM.

Convert all configuration candidates in WebIDL dictionary order before
selection, preserve getter failures, close iterators on failed conversion,
and return independently copied normalized configurations. Share existing
media permissions-policy checks for encrypted-media delegation.

Provide native branding, receiver checks, readonly empty key-status
iteration, pending closed promises and session event handlers. Keep
callback cycles collectible and exceptions page-backed across iframe
teardown. No license messages, usable keys, authenticated certificates,
HDCP protection or successful decryption are fabricated.

Add asynchronous HTMLMediaElement mediaKeys/setMediaKeys integration,
encrypted/waitingforkey handlers, concurrent-operation rejection and
exclusive key attachment. Store authoritative state on native objects so
CDP worlds agree; release attached references on detach and page teardown.
Capture native exposure descriptors and prototypes before page scripts
can replace global constructors; validate value kinds before V8 casts.

No new upstream tests or benchmark changes. Upstream tests pass 1658/1658;
temporary diagnostics pass 123/123, including constructor tampering,
isolated-world attachment, lifecycle and configuration conversion checks.

References:
- Chromium 155.0.8053.0 third_party/blink/renderer/modules/encryptedmedia
- https://w3c.github.io/encrypted-media/
- https://www.apple.com/macbook-neo/specs/

A macOS Chrome CDM capability matrix was not available. Support is an
explicit bounded synthetic profile, not an observed hardware guarantee;
real protected playback and the exact macOS version remain out of scope.
